#20600
The Threshold of the Waste~
   The last grey grass gives out and the ground turns to ash, fine and deep
as snow. The sky is the colour of slate and the sun is a dull coin behind
it. There is no sound at all. Every step leaves a print that the wind fills
in behind you within moments.
~
