#20601
The Ash Dunes~
   Dunes of grey ash roll away to the horizon, rippled by the wind. You sink
to the ankle with every step. Things are buried in the dunes: the top of a
wagon wheel, the tip of a spire, a hand reaching up out of the ash, grey and
perfectly still.
~
