#20615
The Shore of the Dead Lake~
   A lake once lay here, wide and blue. Now it is a basin of grey cracked
mud and salt, ringed by the bleached skeletons of boats. In the centre of
the basin the ground has collapsed into a vast crater, and a column of black
smoke rises from it, unmoving in the wind.
~
